  "output": "Based on the codebase context and prior audit findings, here's the performance analysis with concrete fixes.\n\n## Critical: Memory Leaks\n\n**1. `useCountUp.ts` — RAF loop outlives unmounted component**\n\nThe `requestAnimationFrame` chain has no cancellation. If the component unmounts mid-animation, `setValue` fires on an unmounted component and `ref.current` access continues.\n\n```ts\nuseEffect(() => {\n  if (target === 0) { setValue(0); return; }\n  const start = performance.now();\n  let rafId: number;\n  ref.current?.classList.add('counting');\n  const tick = (now: number) => {\n    const progress = Math.min((now - start) / duration, 1);\n    const eased = 1 - Math.pow(1 - progress, 3);\n    setValue(Math.round(target * eased));\n    if (progress < 1) rafId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);\n    else ref.current?.classList.remove('counting');\n  };\n  rafId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);\n  return () => cancelAnimationFrame(rafId);\n}, [target, duration]);\n```\n\n**2. `useToasts.ts` — dangling `setTimeout` on unmount**\n\nEach toast schedules a `setTimeout(dismissToast, ...)` that isn't cleared if the hook's owner unmounts first, causing a `setState` call on an unmounted tree.\n\n```ts\nconst timers = useRef<Set<ReturnType<typeof setTimeout>>>(new Set());\n\nconst showToast = useCallback((message: string, tone: ToastTone = 'success', durationMs = DEFAULT_DURATION_MS) => {\n  counterRef.current += 1;\n  const id = `toast-${counterRef.current}`;\n  setToasts((prev) => [...prev, { id, message, tone }]);\n  if (durationMs > 0) {\n    const t = setTimeout(() => { dismissToast(id); timers.current.delete(t); }, durationMs);\n    timers.current.add(t);\n  }\n  return id;\n}, [dismissToast]);\n\nuseEffect(() => () => timers.current.forEach(clearTimeout), []);\n```\n\n## Caching Opportunities\n\n**3. `api.ts` never uses `utils/cache.ts`**\n\n`cacheSet`/`cacheGet`/`pruneOldCache` exist but nothing calls them. Read-heavy, rarely-changing endpoints (`phrases`, `outcomes`, `languageSettings`, `platformSettings`) hit the network on every view mount.\n\n```ts\nasync function cachedGet<T>(key: string, path: string, ttlMs = 60_000): Promise<T> {\n  const cached = cacheGet<{ v: T; t: number } | null>(key, null);\n  if (cached && Date.now() - cached.t < ttlMs) return cached.v;\n  const value = await request<T>(path);\n  cacheSet(key, { v: value, t: Date.now() });\n  return value;\n}\n```\nApply to `api.phrases()`, `api.outcomes()`, `api.languageSettings()`, `api.platformSettings()`.\n\n**4. No HTTP cache headers leveraged** — `request()` always sends `Content-Type: application/json` and never sets `Cache-Control`/`If-None-Match`, so the browser HTTP cache can't help either. Worth adding conditional-GET support on the backend + `cache: 'default'` on GETs.\n\n## Redundant Computations\n\n**5. `utils/transcript.ts` — `buildConversationItems` recomputes on every render**\n\nThis does array filtering, mapping, and sorting over full transcript+event arrays. Any call site rendering it inline in JSX reruns it on unrelated re-renders. Wrap call sites:\n\n```ts\nconst items = useMemo(() => buildConversationItems(transcript, events), [transcript, events]);\n```\n\n**6. `formatting.ts` `parseApiDate`/`formatDate`** are called per-row in list views (transcripts, audit log, campaigns) with `toLocaleString` — relatively expensive. If lists are large, memoize per-row via `React.memo` on row components so formatting only reruns when that row's data changes, not on every parent re-render.\n\n## React Re-renders (per prior audit, still applicable)\n\n**7. Monolithic `App.tsx`** — sequential `useEffect` data-loading calls on auth cause cascading re-renders. Batch independent fetches with `Promise.all` and set state once:\n\n```ts\nuseEffect(() => {\n  if (!token) return;\n  Promise.all([api.campaigns(), api.transcripts(), api.platformSettings(), /* ... */])\n    .then(([campaigns, transcripts, settings]) => {\n      setCampaigns(campaigns); setTranscripts(transcripts); setSettings(settings);\n    });\n}, [token]);\n```\n\n**8. List item components (TranscriptsView, CampaignsView) lack `React.memo`** — every parent state change (e.g., a filter keystroke) re-renders all rows. Wrap row components in `React.memo` and ensure row-level callbacks are `useCallback`-stable.\n\n**9. Campaign strategy objects rebuilt every render** — `dialing_strategy` derived objects should be `useMemo`'d off `campaign` rather than reconstructed in the render body.\n\n## Priority order\n1. Fix `useCountUp`/`useToasts` leaks (correctness bugs, not just perf)\n2. Wrap `buildConversationItems` in `useMemo` at call sites\n3. Wire `cachedGet` into `api.ts` for the 4 read-heavy endpoints\n4. Batch `App.tsx` auth-triggered fetches\n5. `React.memo` list rows in Transcripts/Campaigns views\n\nWant me to implement any of these directly? The RAF/timer leak fixes and the `buildConversationItems` memoization are the highest-value, lowest-risk changes — I'd start there.\n",
